15874223"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Swifts","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Hummingbirds","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Swift","source":"Martha's Vineyard species checklist"},{"language":"en","name":"Swifts, Hummingbirds","source":"Martha's Vineyard species checklist"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Apodiformes","confidence":94,"rank":"order","scientificName":"Apodiformes","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":1448},"ottId":609798,"rank":"order","scientificName":"Apodiformes","synonyms":["Trochiliformes"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The Apodiformes is an order, or taxonomic grouping, of birds which traditionally contained three living families—the Apodidae (swifts), the Hemiprocnidae (treeswifts), and the Trochilidae (hummingbirds); however, in the Sibley–Ahlquist taxonomy, this order is elevated to the superorder Apodimorphae, in which hummingbirds are separated into a new order, the Trochiliformes. With nearly 450 species identified to date, it is the most diverse order of birds after the Passeriformes (the \"perching\" birds).","revisionId":1370190717,"title":"Apodiformes","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apodiformes","wikidataId":"Q25950"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"King Parrots","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"King-Parrots","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Alisterus","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Alisterus Mathews, 1911","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2479924},"ottId":682886,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Alisterus","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Alisterus is a genus of medium-sized Australasian parrots, comprising the Australian king parrot (Alisterus scapularis), the Papuan king parrot (A. chloropterus) and the Moluccan king parrot (A. amboinensis). The three species are respectively found in eastern Australia, Papua, the Moluccas and other Indonesian islands.","revisionId":1295689517,"title":"Alisterus","url":"https://